{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And he trusted in YHWH.</b> He did not ask Him for a sign concerning this; but concerning the inheritance of the land he did ask Him for a sign, and said to Him, ״בַּמָּה אֵדַע״." "<b>And He reckoned it to him as righteousness.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, reckoned it to Abram as merit and righteousness on account of the faith that he believed in Him. Another matter: ״בַּמָּה אֵדַע״ — he did not ask Him for a sign, but rather said before Him: Let me know by what merit they will endure in it. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: By the merit of the offerings."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:46.048520043Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}